Subject: [PATCH] Leave out equation code that doesn't compile, like MilkDrop

Local fix against projectM 4.1.7 plus patches 0001–0031. A compile error in any
equation block aborted preset initialization, so the whole preset failed to load.
MilkDrop's CState::RecompileExpressions shows a warning for that block and runs
the rest of the preset: failed init code leaves the q variables (preset init) or
t variables (custom wave/shape init) at zero, and failed per-frame, per-pixel or
per-point code is not run. Do the same, and report each left-out block through
Preset::InitializationWarnings(), ProjectM::PresetInitializationWarningEvent()
and the new C callback projectm_set_preset_initialization_warning_event_callback().
Preset parse errors still fail the load. Tests cover every
block, disabled components and presets without problems.
